1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,749
Immerse follows actual work.

2
00:00:01,819 --> 00:00:08,305
Trace one item from origin to decision and
identify handoffs, re-entry, waiting, and exception

3
00:00:08,375 --> 00:00:13,580
handling. Ask an operator to show the task
and attempt a permitted version yourself.

4
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:17,191
Observe what happens before and
after the proposed solution.

5
00:00:17,261 --> 00:00:22,467
An integration can succeed technically while
adding another queue or another confirmation

6
00:00:22,537 --> 00:00:28,446
step. Capture the entire workflow boundary so
local improvement does not hide additional work

7
00:00:28,516 --> 00:00:29,476
elsewhere.

8
00:00:29,546 --> 00:00:35,029
An agent reads a ticket, looks up the account,
checks a category sheet, assigns a queue, and

9
00:00:35,099 --> 00:00:36,379
records the reason.

10
00:00:36,449 --> 00:00:40,331
Copying takes two minutes, but
waiting for permission can take a day.

11
00:00:40,401 --> 00:00:43,068
The two delays require different interventions.

12
00:00:43,138 --> 00:00:47,917
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

13
00:00:47,987 --> 00:00:50,013
Draw the workflow as ordered steps.

14
00:00:50,083 --> 00:00:53,923
Mark a delay, a handoff, a
duplicate entry, and an exception.

15
00:00:53,993 --> 00:00:59,455
The working map includes intake, account lookup,
category selection, queue assignment, and

16
00:00:59,525 --> 00:01:00,911
decision recording.

17
00:01:00,981 --> 00:01:03,947
A permission delay belongs to access governance.

18
00:01:04,017 --> 00:01:07,750
Repeated category lookup
belongs to routing assistance.

19
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:11,041
Keep both visible, but
test one uncertainty first.

20
00:01:11,111 --> 00:01:15,762
A tool that saves lookup time should not
claim it removed the permission delay.

21
00:01:15,832 --> 00:01:18,008
Why trace the steps after the new tool?

22
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:19,870
A. To add more features B.

23
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:23,353
To identify displaced work
and downstream effects C.

24
00:01:23,423 --> 00:01:25,450
To avoid talking to operators.

25
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:26,992
The best answer is B.

26
00:01:27,062 --> 00:01:30,497
Systems thinking checks the
complete workflow consequence.
